      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrence_County%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The county seat, Lawrenceville, sits in the easternmost corner of the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrence_County%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lawrence County was carved out in 1821 from parts of Crawford and Edwards counties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lawrence_County%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Lawrence Public Library honors Richard “Dick” Poppe by hosting a digital history archive he helped create.",
